  "notes": "お{昼|ひる} is the polite form of {昼|ひる}, commonly used to refer to noon or lunch.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- お{昼|ひる}を{食|た}べる (to eat lunch)\n- お{昼|ひる}ごはん (lunch - more explicit)\n- お{昼|ひる}ごろ (around noon)\n- お{昼|ひる}{休|やす}み (lunch break)\n\nNOTE: While {昼|ひる} alone is grammatically correct, お{昼|ひる} is more commonly used in everyday speech, especially when talking about the meal.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {昼食|ちゅうしょく}: lunch (formal)\n- ランチ: lunch (loanword, often used for restaurant meals)\n- {朝|あさ}ごはん: breakfast\n- {晩|ばん}ごはん: dinner",
